    "164572438470d85add": {
      "type": "accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "164572438495310fd3-0": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What grade titanium are your products made from?",
            "open_by_default": false,
            "text": "<p>All our products are made from titanium, ensuring the product's integrity for a lifetime. Depending on the product, will depend on the Grade of titanium used. Predominantly, SilverAnt uses Grades 1-3 in the manufacture of our products. In addition, all our products are manufactured in our own ISO:9001-2015 factory and are further certified by the FDA and SGS, guaranteeing the highest quality for you, the consumer. To view our certificates, please just send us an email.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "164572438495310fd3-1": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the titanium coated?",
            "open_by_default": false,
            "text": "<p>No, we do not coat our titanium products. We believe in maintaining the integrity of the titanium, ensuring a lifetime of use and protecting the antibacterial, non-allergenic, and non-toxic properties. Sandblasting is powered by compressed air to form a high-speed jet beam to spray the titanium surface. The titanium is then finally washed with water multiple times before drying and packaging. Crystallization is achieved in-house at our factory in a vacuum-sealed oven at high temperatures and pressure. Our anodized products with a variety of colors are achieved using electrical current and an oxide layer on the surface of the titanium.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "164572438495310fd3-2": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the product welding also titanium?",
            "open_by_default": false,
            "text": "<p>Yes, we can't use different metals. Every metal has a different melting point. We can't change it. We can't change the melting point of other materials to the same temperature as titanium and fuse them.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "164572438495310fd3-0",
        "164572438495310fd3-1",
        "164572438495310fd3-2"
      ],
      "settings": {
